==English==
{{rfv}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|arbor||lang=la|tree}} + {{term|vitae|lang=la}}, genitive singular of {{term|vita||lang=la|life}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[arbor]] [[vitae]]|pl=arbor vitae|pl2=arbor vitaes|pl3=arbores vitae}}

# {{context|botany|lang=en}} Any of the evergreen trees known as [[arborvitae]], of the genera ''[[Thuja]]'' and {{taxlink|Thujopsis|genus}}.
#* '''1882''', ''Annual Report of the Minnesota State Horticultural Society'', page 27:
#*: Next spring the owner of the hedge will be very much surprised to find a number of his '''arbor vitae''' deceased, and he will straightway blame himself and his horse? Not he! The nurseyman, sir, must have delivered him some poor stock!
# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} White matter of the [[cerebellum]].
# {{cx|1811|lang=en}} A man's penis.
#* '''2009''', David Nokes, ''Samuel Johnson: A Life'', page 247:
#*: The ''London Evening-Post'' published a fantasy in which Johnson’s ‘''amiable consort''’ became pregnant, ‘''the old lady’s bulk''’ not arising from ‘''the Stamina of his '''arbor vitae'''''’ but from a surfeit of cabbages sent to her {{...}}

